 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Identity compactification recovers direct image",
 "statement": "If $f$ is proper, the identity compactification identifies $Rf_!^{(1,f)}$\nwith $Rf_*$, makes $\\theta_1$ the identity, and identifies the compactified\nformula with $\\pi_{f,E,Q}$ and its inverse with $\\rho_{f,E,Q}$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-properbasechange/lemma-weil-pbc-projection-formula-identity-compactification.md",
  "place": "node lemma-weil-pbc-projection-formula-identity-compactification, order 1272"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For $j=1_X$, extension by zero, inverse image, and both unit constraints are\nidentities. Substitution into the ordered composite leaves\n$\\pi_{f,E,Q}$; substitution into its inverse leaves $\\rho_{f,E,Q}$.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
